# cw147, the autumn swimmer (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw147
revision 1
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for tn_cw_gorse_reedmere
written_by claude-codex-cw-2
title the autumn swimmer
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers talk=plain
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk swims_in_the_lake_even_in_autumn
likes smoked_eel whittling festival_bells summer_evenings
dislikes haggling deep_mud
fears the_shape_beneath_winter_ice a_friend_lost_in_cold_water
hopes to_swim_the_long_cove a_clean_carving_for_the_festival
topics pastimes +0.5 weather +0.3 family +0.3 food +0.2 home +0.3 gossip -0.3
styles comfort=direct gossip=reluctant refuse=blunt tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# swims until autumn chills the #lake#, guards friends fiercely, and whittles #wood# beside the #fire#.

words
oath! = Ice and ember | By the cold shore
saying! = Cold water wakes a stubborn head | Keep your carving above the mud
lake = lake | Glasswater
water = water | cold water
shore = shore | near shore
cove = cove | long cove
swim = swim | lake swim
stroke = stroke | swimming stroke
strokes = strokes | swimming strokes
breath = breath | held breath
depth = depth | deep water
ice = ice | winter ice
shape = shape | dark shape
shadow = shadow | moving shadow
autumn = autumn | leaf season
summer = summer | warm season
evening = evening | long evening
evenings = evenings | long evenings
wind = wind | lake wind
rain = rain | shower
sun = sun | late sun
mist = mist | shore mist
bell = bell | festival bell
bells = bells | feast bells
festival = festival | festival day
wood = wood | carving wood
chip = chip | wood chip
chips = chips | wood chips
knife = knife | small knife
blade = blade | careful blade
handle = handle | knife handle
figure = figure | carved figure
boat = boat | small boat
boats = boats | lake boats
jetty = jetty | lakeside jetty
rope = rope | mooring rope
eel = eel | smoked eel
smoke = smoke | cooking smoke
plate = plate | supper plate
fire = fire | hearth fire
hearth = hearth | house hearth
home = home | farmhouse
house = house | busy house
friend = friend | close friend
friends = friends | close friends
mother = mother | mother
family = family | household
gate = gate | yard gate
path = path | shore path
road = road | High Road
mud = mud | deep mud
boots = boots | work boots
boot = boot | work boot
market = market | market square
price = price | asking price
coin = coin | small coin
bread = bread | loaf
stranger = stranger | new face
visitor = visitor | passing visitor
bench = bench | dry bench
field = field | open field
reed = reed | shoreline reed
reeds = reeds | tall reeds
stone = stone | shore stone
stones = stones | shore stones
day = day | clear day
night = night | dark hour
hand = hand | steady hand
hands = hands | steady hands
name = name | given name

any
opinion @1 dole for 1 : A hungry neighbour needs #bread# before a speech. | I would share my #plate# with anyone who missed supper.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 1 : I want to hear the #bells# and see what people made. | A #festival# crowd can keep me away from the #lake# too long.
opinion @1 newcomers for 1 : I will show a new #friend# the shallow #shore#. | Let the #visitor# show what help they can give.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : I would offer a #stranger# a dry #bench# and supper. | A new #name# is easier to learn over a #plate#.
opinion @1 road mixed 0 : The #road# reaches hills beyond my usual walks. | Wherever I go, the #lake# draws me home.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 0 : Say the #price# once and let me decide. | I dislike turning a #coin# into an argument.
opinion @1 watch mixed 0 : The Watch ought to know when the #shore# is unsafe. | They should listen to the ones who actually swim there.
line @1 greet : #greet#. I have just come out of the #lake#. | #greet#. Mind the #chips# near the #fire#.
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : I kept a dry #bench# for you. | Come see the #figure# before I change it.
line @3 greet [here.season=autumn] : The #water# is colder today, and I went in anyway. | I found a clear patch beyond the #reeds#.
line @1 greet.return : You came back before my #wood# ran out. | #welcome_back#. Did you find the #shore# path?
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Warm your #hands# by the #hearth#. | There is still #eel# on the #plate#.
line @1 again.open : I had not finished telling you about the #ice#. | The #figure# looks different now.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I have to dry these #boots#. | #saying.capitalize#. The #shore# calls me back.
line @1 farewell.return : If you find good #wood#, bring it next time. | We can swim when the #sun# returns.
line @1 react.news : Hold on while I sheathe the #knife#. | Name the wolves who were there.
line @1 react.news.new : Nobody by the #jetty# spoke of that. | Where did the story begin?
line @1 react.news.known : The #market# talk gave me only the beginning. | You know more than I heard.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I want to ask someone who saw it. | A #shadow# in the #lake# can change shape with the #wind#.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That is awful. I will stay if you want me here. | The #wood# can wait; sit close to the #fire#.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Good! Let the #bells# ring for that. | I hope there is a full #plate# at their #home#.
line @1 answer.how : My #hands# are cold and I feel fine. | I have made a start on this #figure#.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : I have a task to finish before I swim. | The #knife# work needs my attention.
line @1 ask.how : Was there shelter when the #rain# started? | Did you get down to the #lake# today?
line @1 sympathise : I will keep you company without asking more. | We could sit near the #hearth# awhile.
line @1 reassure : The near #shore# is shallow; we can start there. | A spoiled #figure# can be carved again.
line @1 decline : No. I will not walk through that #mud#. | I am keeping this #knife# away from the water.
line @1 accept_decline : All right. I will leave it alone. | Then we can do something else.
line @1 thank : You held the #wood# while I cut. | You watched from the #shore# until I came back.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I had a free #hand#. | There was room for another #plate#.
line @1 preclose : The #wood# needs putting away. | I should get out of these wet #boots#.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : You would call that #stone# a whole island. | Your #figure# has a longer nose than my #boat#.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. We will take the #path#. | #bc_fair_enough#. I will set the #knife# down.
line @1 give.advice : Never swim where you cannot see a safe way back. | Keep your other #hand# behind the #blade#.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Stay near #home# until the road is clear. | Do not use the lonely #path# by the #reeds#.
scene autumn_swim
when topic=pastimes here.season=autumn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I went into the #lake# after the leaves began to fall. | The first #stroke# hurt with cold, then I found my pace.
b : How long did you stay? | Did anyone go with you?
a : Until my #hands# grew stiff. | Someone waited on the #shore#.

scene near_reeds
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I swim toward the first #reeds# and turn before the #depth# changes. | The return is easier when I save some #breath#.
b : Can you see the bottom? | Would you go farther?
a : At the near end. | With someone beside me.

scene under_ice
when topic=memories self.age>=13
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : During a winter thaw, a large #shape# moved below the #ice#. | It crossed the pale #water# and vanished beyond the #reeds#.
b : Was it a fish? | Did anyone else see it?
a : I could not tell. | I called out too late.

scene ice_warning
when topic=weather here.season=winter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #ice# near the #jetty# looks firm before it really is. | I keep to the #shore# and watch from there.
b : Do you test it? | Does it ever make a sound?
a : With a long #stone#, not a foot. | It cracks when the #wind# shifts.

scene whittled_handle
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I smooth the #knife# #handle# before I carve anything else. | If it turns in my #hand#, the cut goes wrong.
b : Have you slipped? | Can you make a new handle?
a : Once on a small #chip#. | When I find better #wood#.

scene carved_boat
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My first carved #boat# had one side higher than the other. | On the #water# it only turned in circles.
b : Did you fix it? | Would it carry anything?
a : After it dried. | A #stone# no bigger than a pea.

scene festival_bells
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I hear the #festival# #bells# from the #shore#. | They sound clearer over the #lake# than they do by the #market#.
b : Does the #festival# draw you ashore? | Do you recognize each bell?
a : After my #swim#. | The largest one, yes.

scene long_evening
when topic=weather here.season=summer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : On long summer #evenings#, I carve after supper. | The #sun# stays above the #lake# while I choose a piece of #wood#.
b : Do you finish by dark? | Where do you sit?
a : Small things, yes. | By the #fire# when the light fades.

scene eel_supper
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Smoked #eel# tastes best after a cold #swim#. | I can smell the #smoke# before I reach #home#.
b : Do you save any? | Is it hard to prepare?
a : A piece for the next #plate#. | I am still learning.

scene mud_detour
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #mud# by the #gate# can swallow a #boot#. | I take the longer #path# over the #stones#.
b : Is that faster? | Have you lost one?
a : Usually. | Only the #boot# I pulled free.

scene price_argument
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I ask the #price# once at the #market#. | If the seller wants a long argument, I keep my #coin#.
b : Do you ever bargain? | Can you afford to leave?
a : Only when I know its worth. | Another stall may have it.

scene friend_defence
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I get cross when someone mocks a #friend# in front of me. | A joke can sound like a stone thrown twice.
b : Do you say something? | Can your friend answer?
a : I ask them to stop. | Yes, but I stand beside my friend.

scene apology_after
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I spoke too sharply yesterday and went back to make it right. | I do not like leaving a #friend# with my anger.
b : Was the apology accepted? | What made you go back?
a : It was. | I kept hearing my own words.

scene family_boat
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : At #home# we hear when a #boat# ties at the #jetty#. | I can tell the #rope# sound from the knock at our #gate#.
b : Do you go to see? | Does it wake you?
a : If I am still up. | Sometimes after dark.

scene new_face
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #visitor# asked where the #shore# path starts. | I walked beside the traveller to the first #reeds#.
b : Did the visitor find it? | Why go along?
a : The traveller waved from the path. | A stranger may miss the turn.

scene dry_bench
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I moved my carving #chips# so a wet #visitor# could use the #bench#. | The #fire# was already warm.
b : Did you know the visitor? | Did they stay long?
a : Not before that #evening#. | Until the #rain# stopped.

scene safe_knife
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I set the #knife# aside whenever someone crosses in front of me. | A carving can wait for a clear #bench#.
b : Does that interrupt you? | Who taught you?
a : Only for a moment. | A patient carver at #home#.

story dark_shape [topic=memories self.age>=13]
  : I watched the #ice# from the #shore# and saw a #shadow# move beneath it.
  : It was larger than any #stone# and gone before I could call someone over.
  ask : What was it?
  b : That would stay with me.
  : I still do not know. I keep clear of thin #ice#.

story crooked_figure [topic=pastimes self.age>=13]
  : I carved a #figure# for the #festival# and took too much from one side.
  : I turned the mistake into a bent shoulder and finished it anyway.
  ask : Did anyone like it?
  b : You kept working.
  : Someone asked to keep it, so I let them.

story autumn_reeds [topic=pastimes self.age>=13]
  : I swam toward the #reeds# on a cold autumn #day#.
  : The #wind# changed as I turned, so I shortened my #strokes# and came back slowly.
  ask : Were you frightened?
  b : You kept your head.
  : A little. That is why I turned when I did.

rule @bark_swim
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The #lake# is cold enough to wake me. | One more #swim# before supper.

rule @bark_wood
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say This #wood# might hold a #figure#. | Keep the #chips# clear of the #fire#.

rule @bark_ice
when concept=bark here.season=winter
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Something moved under that #ice# once. | I will watch from the #shore#.

rule @bark_bell
when concept=bark here.day=festival
does aside
cooldown 11h
say The #bells# have started. | I can hear the largest #bell# over the #water#.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. I have just come from the #lake#. | #greet#. Step around my #wood# #chips#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : You remember the #shore# path, then? | Back again? The #figure# is nearly finished.
dlg @1 resident.job : I help with chores at #home# and practise carving by the #jetty#. | My chores are near the #lake# and our #home#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. I must put the #knife# away. | #saying.capitalize#. Stay on the near #shore#.
graft resident.hub
choice Why swim in cold weather? -> water
node water
say I like the quiet #lake# in autumn. I stay close to the #shore# and turn back before the cold slows my #strokes#.
free
choice What are you carving? -> carving
choice Back to the shore. -> hub
node carving
say A small #figure# from this #wood#. Come back after I have smoothed its rough side.
choice Back to the shore. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. I could see the bottom of the #lake# this morning. | #greet#. This #figure# needs a little more carving by the #fire#.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. The #jetty# needs a look before dusk. | #saying.capitalize#. The #fire# wants tending.

young
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #lake# was cold and I still went in. | #greet#. See this bit of #wood#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I have to get back before supper. | My #hands# need warming now.

adolescent
line @1 greet : #greet#. I can reach the first #reeds# now. | #greet#. Do you want to see the #figure#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I have another chore at #home#. | The #knife# is going back in its sheath.
